                <pb facs="1046" n="926" xml:id="pg926"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State Loomis to Minister
                        Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(In view of Mr. Bowen’s telegram of 30th ultimo, Mr. Loomis instructs him to
                    formally protest both orally and in writing against summary proceedings of
                    Venezuelan Government dispossessing New York and Bermudez Company of its
                    property without any hearing and directly in government’s interest, and notify
                    government of grave concern with which United States Government will regard any
                    illegal action against American company.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
